On Thu, Sep 16, 2010 at 5:19 PM, Lindar <lindarthebard@yahoo.com> wrote:
> Your accent would be so lovely if you'd just tap those R's. ;-;

Maybe in theory, but I'm not very good at tapped Rs actually.

> Do you have a list of these goofy songs?

Nope I haven't organized what I've uploaded much at all.  I was very
surprised recently to find that a lot of my songs weren't on YouTube
yet.  Jonathan Jones was suggesting to me that I should make a
playlist of my educational videos, so I guess I'll also make a
playlist of songs if I get a chance.  (I guess this video will go on
both!)  There's probably some I sing to myself all the time that I
still haven't recorded.  There's lots more that I made up for a second
and then forgot about -- like often I think of bad translations of pop
songs if they get stuck in my head.

OH!  I don't think there's any recordings of "mi ba te tinbe".  That's
more of a chant than a song.  It just goes: ".i mi ca minde .i mi ba
te tinbe" (I am now commanding.  I will be obeyed.) over & over.  I'll
record that today.

> They're amazingly catchy, and I would love to put music to them.

Thanks!  I'd love to have some musical accompaniment.  If you make the
music and show me (like with a score) how the song should go with it
I'll gladly record a vocal track to match the music.  Except I don't
have any decent recording setup these days. :(  (My soundcard I
usually use is only Firewire, and my new netbook is only USB.)

Someday maybe we can put out a Lojbanic CD together and make
millions^wthousands^Whundreds^Wseveral dollars! :D

